From: axon7-build <axon7-build@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:55:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 43/45] axon7: RIL Parcel ABI shim; Bluetooth SoC property and
 extldo label

- rild aborted with stack corruption in vendor_ril_send_hook_response:
  libril-qc-qmi-1 keeps Android 8 sized Parcels on its stack. Its eight
  Parcel imports are renamed to android::PaRcel, which libril_parcel_shim
  implements with a heap Parcel.
- libbt-vendor reads vendor.qcom.bluetooth.soc (qcom.bluetooth.soc could not
  be set by vendor_init); hal_bluetooth_qti writes bt_qca6174/extldo.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FVN6i29oeF8XZDRKkkCQqG
Change-Id: I3a6cff88f25efb7a8b902955cecd50873de16270
